# No domain yet? Two ways to still get HTTPS (the camera scanner and the login
# cookie both REQUIRE it). Pick ONE block, replace 203.0.113.5 with the server's
# public IP, and put it in Caddy's config (/etc/caddy/Caddyfile).

# --- A) Recommended: a real, free hostname made from the IP ------------------
# sslip.io answers DNS for names like 203-0-113-5.sslip.io with 203.0.113.5, so
# Caddy can get a genuine Let's Encrypt certificate: no browser warning, and the
# app installs as a PWA. (Dots in the IP become dashes.) Needs ports 80 and 443
# reachable from the internet and not used by another program.
203-0-113-5.sslip.io {
    encode gzip
    header {
        Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
        -Server
    }
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

# --- B) Fallback: self-signed certificate on the bare IP ---------------------
# Works without any DNS, but every browser shows a "not private" warning once
# (Advanced -> Proceed), and the offline/PWA install feature is unavailable.
# https://203.0.113.5 {
#     tls internal
#     encode gzip
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
